# Trivy allowlist.
#
# Rules for this file:
#   1. Every entry carries a CVE, a reason, and an expiry date.
#   2. An entry expires. Trivy stops honouring it after `exp:`, so a
#      suppression cannot quietly become permanent.
#   3. "It is noisy" is not a reason. The reason must say why the
#      vulnerability is not exploitable in Meridian specifically, or what is
#      blocking the upgrade and when it is expected.
#
# The release gate already passes `--ignore-unfixed`, so anything without an
# available patch is out of scope and does not belong here. This file is only
# for vulnerabilities that DO have a fix which we are consciously deferring.
#
# Format:
#   CVE-YYYY-NNNNN exp:YYYY-MM-DD
#   # why, and what unblocks it
#
# Currently empty — nothing has been consciously accepted. The counts from
# the first scan are recorded in docs/MEASUREMENTS.md.
